    "analysis_type": "paradigm_network",
    "rationale": "Only two small construction families are defensible. (1) 4cnr/X and 4e/X form a clear minimal pair in the same frame with stable compositional meanings: the first morpheme contributes the spatial operator ('each corner of face' vs. 'each edge of face') and the second slot is a face value, whose members are declared by the standalone face key entries F/Bk/L/R/T/Bo. (2) FA6/<startF> and FA2/<startF> likewise form a minimal pair in the same frame: the first morpheme contributes the whole procedure variant ('cool cloth ... then fan all 6 in sequence' vs. 'cool cloth ... then fan start face plus opposite only') and the second slot is again a face value, declared by the same standalone face entries. Other apparent recurrences are rejected: ?<motif> and ?<m1>/<m2>:<q> do not provide a clean shared frame with predictable part meanings, and the remaining symbols are best kept lexical. Symbols used only as declared fillers remain in lexical_symbols, as required.",
